Based on the search results, here's relevant information about using Shopify theme app extensions with app blocks on product pages:

## Accessing Product Data in App Blocks

App blocks have access to standard Liquid objects like product, collection, and cart, but only within the context of the current page.

## Passing product.id to JavaScript

To pass the `product.id` from your Liquid template to your JavaScript file, you can use HTML data attributes. In the app-block.liquid file, you can render an HTML element with data attributes like `<image-gallery data-id="{{ block.id }}">` and include product information such as `<p>{{ product.id }}</p>`.

Your JavaScript widget can then access this data:

```javascript
class ImageGallery extends HTMLElement {
  connectedCallback() {
    const productId = this.getAttribute('data-product-id');
    // Use productId for API calls
  }
}
```

## App Block Structure

Everything above the `{% schema %}` tag is the body of the app block where you define what your block will render. The body is built using HTML markup and Liquid. You can specify a JavaScript file to load from the assets folder, and these assets will only be loaded if the block is present on the page, and only loaded once regardless of how many times the block is present.

This approach allows you to embed product data directly in HTML attributes for your widget to consume via the DOM API.


